data birkhoff_von_neumann_1936_citation_note: String = "Cited upstream: Birkhoff, G. and von Neumann, J., 'The Logic of Quantum Mechanics', Annals of Mathematics volume 37 number 4, pages 823-843, 1936 (doi 10.2307/1968621). Locator is the publisher DOI redirect; JSTOR landing at the resolved target returned HTTP 403 to this host on 2026-08-03, so full text was not read here — the DOI is the durable anchor, not a page we asserted from memory.\n\nWHAT THIS MODULE OWNS. The cited 1936 formalism only: quantum propositions form an orthomodular lattice, Boolean algebras are distributive, and the quantum lattice is not distributive in general. It does NOT own experimental apparatus rows, intensity profiles, or which-path illumination outcomes — those are independently governed upstream subjects."

data quantum_proposition_lattice_non_distributive_note: String = "Authority claim carried at citation boundary: the quantum proposition lattice modeled in the 1936 formalism refutes the distributive law meet(a, join(b, c)) = join(meet(a, b), meet(a, c)) that Boolean algebras satisfy. Downstream observing layers derive a located counterexample witness for a finite Bach et al. 2013 scenario; this module does not execute an experiment or transcribe a numeric diffraction curve."
